+ *
+ * pathprobe_path_rejected_hook: called when new_path is dominated.
+ *   new_path will be pfree'd after hook returns; snapshot all needed fields.
+ *   dominated_by is the old path in rel->pathlist that dominates new_path
+ *   (the one add_path() stopped at); it stays in the pathlist.
+ *
+ * pathprobe_path_accepted_hook: called when new_path survives.
+ *   dominated_list: paths displaced by new_path (may be NIL).
+ *
+ * pathprobe_path_removed_hook: called after the rejected hook when new_path
+ *   had removed old paths from the pathlist before an old path was found to
+ *   dominate it.  removed_list is never NIL; its paths (and new_path) are
+ *   freed after the hook returns, IndexPaths excepted.
